				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Sky): Add exception signature throttling to PostHog bridge\n\nExceptions share the `$exception` event-name slot in posthog-js, so a burst of CSP refusals/console.error/unhandledrejection callbacks during workbench boot would blow through the 10/10s rate limit. Add a secondary throttle layer keyed by the first 200 chars of the error message.\n\nUnique exceptions still reach PostHog while bursts of the same error collapse into one. Both regular and exception drop counts are now reported in the `land:sky:throttle-dropped` event for visibility.\n\nThis follows the previous throttling commit (24e76da) which added the basic per-event-name throttle for non-exception events.",
			"SHA": "f601c0a884535251332d05d5a36cf874c147af8d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T18:45:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Sky): Upgrade Astro and @astrojs/compiler-rs dependencies\n\nBump astro from 6.1.8 to 6.1.9 and @astrojs/compiler-rs from 0.1.7 to 0.1.8 in package.json. These are patch releases containing upstream bug fixes and performance improvements.",
			"SHA": "a29752071da8a74ad52c469b8daa4515a0c17d1f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T18:18:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				81,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Sky): Delegate build pipeline to Output plugins, move phase advancement into workbench.js\n\nMajor refactoring of Sky's astro.config.ts build pipeline:\n\n**Plugin delegation:** Inline Steps 1-7, 10-12, and 14 are now delegated to a plugin-based `BuildPipeline` and `ApplyPlugins` system under `Element/Output/Source/Plugin/`. This moves ~400 lines of copy/patch logic into reusable, testable plugins with a consistent interface. Steps 8, 8b, 9, and 13 remain inline (documented in comments) because they require Mountain-specific knowledge or spawn external commands.\n\n**Phase advancement relocation:** The `_A(phase)` function is now injected directly into workbench.js rather than living in a top-level Astro `<script>` block. This prevents Astro/Vite's chunk hoisting from blocking the async import and deferring phase advances past Mountain's 8s/23s fallback timers. Duplicate advances are safe since Mountain rejects backwards/same-phase transitions.\n\n**Removed ext-registry-probe:** The post-boot probe for `globalThis.monaco.extensions` always reported `monacoExtensionsApi:false` in modern VS Code (the API isn't on globalThis). Removed as noise; can be re-enabled via env-driven define if needed.\n\n**Other changes:** Gate missing browser bundle warnings behind `LAND_WARN_MISSING_BROWSER_BUNDLES=true` to keep default output clean. Add NodeModules and Addons configuration sections to the pipeline.",
			"SHA": "4c3a80c40733108c47b2d6161f4a3595204a963c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-22T17:25:17Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
